{"id": "EUVD-2026-93218", "enisaUuid": "4a5ff326-59c0-3171-a42f-a86c34e44e8f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: RFCOMM: avoid socket lock inversion in listener cleanup\n\nrfcomm_sock_cleanup_listen() closes unaccepted child sockets through\nrfcomm_sock_close(), which takes the child socket lock before\nrfcomm_dlc_close() acquires rfcomm_mutex. The RFCOMM worker takes these\nlocks in reverse order while handling connections and DLC state changes,\nso lockdep reports a possible deadlock.\n\nClose dequeued children without taking their socket lock. The accept queue\nowns a reference to each child, and bt_accept_dequeue() locks the child\nwhile unlinking it and clearing its parent pointer.\n\nDropping the child lock makes it important to prevent a concurrent\nrfcomm_connect_ind() from enqueueing a new child after cleanup observes an\nempty queue. Set a listening socket to BT_CLOSED while its lock is still\nheld, before dropping the lock and draining the queue. The state check in\nrfcomm_connect_ind() then rejects new children once cleanup starts.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:17:01", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eb4adaa46e4c9e6efa7be3ce06398f4d7c39b57c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4aafb47301a799d3e01230d6568c4e93524e1523", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c741977e413f5b49d306700820fb55ccb8269f5a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c6792c441767256030606eb82dca5d5fc360dd9a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bfce253f039eb5f58b810af267942a9f59207254", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/18174b166547ef41973cc19feb5ef9cab39a8def", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/801fb950cae7048eb7d83b18857d1ca37b8cd5a4"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98290", "GHSA-vgg6-jhr8-9c2m"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "16a4d78b-daee-364d-9a1f-ef38102eb0c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "18712171-a272-3a9e-9617-dc5cc1f054dc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "1feef1cf-5581-365f-a2c1-f071f1b849b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b7ce436a5d798bc59e71797952566608a4b4626b <bfce253f039eb5f58b810af267942a9f59207254"}, {"id": "22594a29-c0e7-3535-84ac-efd9819fff42", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "5885577e-2047-3b6c-96d6-5f4fb365bc7b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "5acc1e71-85c0-3132-9ac8-9b78eef70ef7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b7ce436a5d798bc59e71797952566608a4b4626b <801fb950cae7048eb7d83b18857d1ca37b8cd5a4"}, {"id": "5b81f966-095b-30b4-a740-a5fc00f3b656", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b7ce436a5d798bc59e71797952566608a4b4626b <18174b166547ef41973cc19feb5ef9cab39a8def"}, {"id": "7348ec8c-013e-361a-b0ba-33e59e78c3e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "75e03f1b-63f0-361c-9378-9dd7636679ad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b7ce436a5d798bc59e71797952566608a4b4626b <c741977e413f5b49d306700820fb55ccb8269f5a"}, {"id": "920ab789-2578-34f1-843f-cfe86bfc210f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "a0d97704-f65b-3243-8cb7-dfe69b2410d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b7ce436a5d798bc59e71797952566608a4b4626b <eb4adaa46e4c9e6efa7be3ce06398f4d7c39b57c"}, {"id": "ab9c7c09-0251-3d26-8ca8-44fdb71d32c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_